findings.body:
Returning `Access-Control-Allow-Credentials: true` together with `Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *` (or an arbitrary incoming origin) violates the CORS specification. Browsers will refuse to expose the response to JavaScript when this pair is present. The prior implementation correctly gated both the specific origin and the credentials flag behind the allow-list.

```suggestion
  if (!origin) {
    return { "Access-Control-Allow-Origin": "*" };
  }
  // validate origin against an allow-list before returning credentials
  return {
    "Access-Control-Allow-Origin": origin,
    "Access-Control-Allow-Credentials": "true",
    Vary: "Origin",
  };
```
